.TH SDL_HINT_THREAD_FORCE_REALTIME_TIME_CRITICAL 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_THREAD_FORCE_REALTIME_TIME_CRITICAL \- Specifies whether
.BR SDL_THREAD_PRIORITY_TIME_CRITICAL
should be treated as realtime.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_THREAD_FORCE_REALTIME_TIME_CRITICAL \(dqSDL_THREAD_FORCE_REALTIME_TIME_CRITICAL\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
On some platforms, like Linux, a realtime priority thread may be subject to restrictions that require special handling by the application\[char46] This hint exists to let SDL know that the app is prepared to handle said restrictions\[char46]
.PP
On Linux, SDL will apply the following configuration to any thread that becomes realtime:
.PP

\(bu The SCHED_RESET_ON_FORK bit will be set on the scheduling policy,
.PP
\(bu An RLIMIT_RTTIME budget will be configured to the rtkit specified limit\[char46]
.PP
\(bu Exceeding this limit will result in the kernel sending SIGKILL to the app, refer to the man pages for more information\[char46]
.PP
The variable can be set to the following values:
.PP

\(bu \(dq0\(dq: default platform specific behaviour
.PP
\(bu \(dq1\(dq: Force
.BR SDL_THREAD_PRIORITY_TIME_CRITICAL
to a realtime scheduling policy
.PP
This hint should be set before calling
.BR SDL_SetCurrentThreadPriority ()

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

